@startuml
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam dpi 150
scale max 2200 width
hide empty members
legend bottom
aggregate root: entry point to the aggregate's entities.
external reference: identity of an object from another context.
Dependencies labeled with Id represent references by identifier.
All value objects have no identity and are immutable.
Values are validated on construction; changes create a new value.
Equality compares attributes, except for Timestamp (UTC instant).
CalendarDate represents a valid date without a time or time zone.
endlegend
title SkyCrop - Users, Authentication and Subscriptions
abstract class User <<aggregate root>> {
-id: Long
-name: Name
-email: EmailAddress
-createdAt: Timestamp
+register(): void

}
class UserProfile <<aggregate root>> {
-userId: Long
-id: Long
-phone: PhoneNumber [0..1]
-address: PostalAddress [0..1]
+updateInformation(): void
}
class Subscription <<aggregate root>> {
-userId: Long
-id: Long
-period: SubscriptionPeriod
-type: SubscriptionType
-status: SubscriptionStatus
+activate(): void
+renew(): void
+cancel(): void
+isActive(): boolean
+hasFeature(feature: String): boolean
}
class Farmer  {

+managePlots(): void
+manageDrones(): void
+viewReports(): void
}
class Agronomist  {
-professionalLicense: String
+analyzeCrop(): void
+managePlots(): void
+generateReport(): void
}
class Payment <<aggregate root>> {
-subscriptionId: Long
-id: Long
-amount: Money
-paymentDate: Timestamp
-method: PaymentMethod
-status: PaymentStatus
+initiate(): void
+authorize(): boolean
+reject(): void
+refund(): void
}
interface PaymentProcessor  {

+process(payment: Payment): boolean
+authorize(payment: Payment): boolean
}
class Account <<aggregate root>> {
-userId: Long
-id: Long
-username: Username
-passwordHash: PasswordHash
-status: AccountStatus
+create(): void
+authenticate(): boolean
+deactivate(): void
}
interface AuthenticationService  {

+authenticate(account: Account): boolean
+verifyTwoFactor(code: String): boolean
+recoverAccount(code: String): boolean
}
interface EmailService  {

+sendVerificationCode(email: EmailAddress): void
+sendRecoveryCode(email: EmailAddress): void
}
class TwoFactorAuthentication  {
-id: Long
-enabled: boolean
-verifiedAt: Timestamp [0..1]
+generateCode(): String
+verify(code: String): boolean
}
class RecoveryCode  {
-id: Long
-code: String
-used: boolean
-expiresAt: Timestamp
+generate(): String
+validate(): boolean
+use(): void
}
enum SubscriptionStatus {
ACTIVE
EXPIRED
CANCELLED
PENDING
}
enum SubscriptionType {
BASIC
PROFESSIONAL
COOPERATIVE
}
enum PaymentMethod {
CARD
TRANSFER
OTHER
}
enum PaymentStatus {
PENDING
AUTHORIZED
REJECTED
REFUNDED
}
enum AccountStatus {
ACTIVE
INACTIVE
LOCKED
}
class EmailAddress <<value object>> {
-value: String {readOnly}

}
class Money <<value object>> {
-amount: Decimal {readOnly}
-currency: String {readOnly}
+add(other: Money): Money
+subtract(other: Money): Money
}
note right of Money
Immutable; equality compares amount and currency.
add/subtract require the same currency
and return a new Money value.
end note
User <|-- Farmer
User <|-- Agronomist
UserProfile ..> User : userId
Subscription ..> User : userId
Account ..> User : userId
Payment ..> Subscription : subscriptionId
Subscription --> SubscriptionStatus : status
Subscription --> SubscriptionType : type
Payment --> PaymentMethod : method
Payment --> PaymentStatus : status
PaymentProcessor ..> Payment : processes
Account --> AccountStatus : status
Account "1" *-- "0..1" TwoFactorAuthentication : uses
Account "1" *-- "0..*" RecoveryCode : has
AuthenticationService ..> Account : authenticates
AuthenticationService ..> TwoFactorAuthentication : verifies
AuthenticationService ..> RecoveryCode : recovers
EmailService ..> TwoFactorAuthentication : sends code
EmailService ..> RecoveryCode : sends code
EmailService ..> EmailAddress
User "1" *-- "1" EmailAddress : email
Payment "1" *-- "1" Money : amount
class Name <<value object>> {
-value: String {readOnly}
}
note right of Name
Non-empty text after trimming outer whitespace.
Preserves the name's characters and original case.
Does not require a specific word count.
end note
class Timestamp <<value object>> {
-value: DateTimeOffset {readOnly}
}
note right of Timestamp
Valid instant with an explicit time zone offset.
Equality and ordering compare the UTC instant.
end note
User "1" *-- "1" Name : name
User ..> Timestamp : temporal values
Payment ..> Timestamp : temporal values
TwoFactorAuthentication ..> Timestamp : temporal values
RecoveryCode ..> Timestamp : temporal values
class PhoneNumber <<value object>> {
-value: String {readOnly}
}
note right of PhoneNumber
International format: + followed by up to 15 digits.
No whitespace or separators in the stored value.
Syntax validation does not verify number ownership.
end note
class PostalAddress <<value object>> {
-value: String {readOnly}
}
note right of PostalAddress
Non-empty address text with outer whitespace removed.
No required postal code or fixed address structure.
end note
class CalendarDate <<value object>> {
-value: Date {readOnly}
}
class SubscriptionPeriod <<value object>> {
-startDate: CalendarDate {readOnly}
-endDate: CalendarDate {readOnly}
+contains(date: CalendarDate): boolean
}
note right of SubscriptionPeriod
Valid dates; endDate > startDate.
Interval [startDate, endDate).
renew replaces the period with a new value.
end note
UserProfile "1" *-- "0..1" PhoneNumber : phone
UserProfile "1" *-- "0..1" PostalAddress : address
Subscription "1" *-- "1" SubscriptionPeriod : period
SubscriptionPeriod "1" *-- "2" CalendarDate : boundaries
note bottom of TwoFactorAuthentication
verifiedAt may be absent before verification.
RecoveryCode expires when now >= expiresAt.
end note
class Username <<value object>> {
-value: String {readOnly}
}
note right of Username
Non-empty text after trimming outer whitespace.
Preserves case; equality compares the stored value.
Account uniqueness follows the identity policy.
end note
class PasswordHash <<value object>> {
-encodedValue: String {readOnly}
}
note right of PasswordHash
Non-empty encoded output of the credential hasher.
Contains the algorithm parameters required by the verifier.
Never stores plaintext or appears in HTTP responses.
Equality compares the encoded representation.
end note
Account "1" *-- "1" Username : username
Account "1" *-- "1" PasswordHash : passwordHash
@enduml
